WISE_OUTGOING_ENABLED=Enable outgoing payment preparation
WISE_OUTGOING_ENABLEDTooltip=When ON, supplier invoices expose Wise transfer preparation (draft transfer created via API, funded manually in the Wise dashboard). Requires the transfers#state-change subscription for automatic status write-back.
SLYCUSTOM_TAB_SHIPSGO=ShipsGo
SLYCUSTOM_SHIPSGO_SECTION=ShipsGo connection
WISE_WEBHOOK_IPCHECK=Webhook source IP allowlist
WISE_WEBHOOK_IPCHECKTooltip=Reject webhook deliveries whose source IP is outside the Wise egress networks (45.129.54.0/24, 45.129.55.0/24 per docs.wise.com). While no verification key is available this is the authentication that lets deliveries be ingested at all; once the key is saved, signature verification takes over. Only REMOTE_ADDR is checked, so a reverse proxy or CDN in front of the site will block every delivery.
WISE_WEBHOOK_IPLIST=Additional source IPs / CIDRs
WISE_WEBHOOK_IPLISTTooltip=One IP or CIDR per line, e.g. 18.184.0.0/16. Lines starting with # are comments; invalid lines are dropped silently. This list is ADDED to the hardcoded baseline (Wise documented ranges + AWS /16s seen in production); it is not a replacement. Useful when Wise starts delivering from a new range: copy the source IP from a rejected/ dump and add the appropriate /16 here. The textarea is only shown when the source IP allowlist is enabled.
WiseIplistInactive=Enable the source IP allowlist above to edit the additional addresses.
WISE_IPCHECK_ACTIVE=Source IP allowlist active: deliveries from the Wise egress networks are ingested even without signature verification (interim mode).
WISE_SIGNATURE_KEYTooltip=The subscription public key Wise generates automatically. Look for it on the subscription detail page in Wise Settings > Developer tools > Webhooks, then save it to DOL_DATA_ROOT/wise_webhook/verification_key.pem (or use the fetch button when the subscriptions API is reachable).

