WISE_DIAG_GUIDE=How to check whether Wise is really pushing
WiseDiagStep1=1. Test the URL from this server
WiseDiagStep1Desc=Click "Run self-test" below. It POSTs to %s from the server itself and reports the HTTP status. A 404 means the file is not on disk; a timeout means DNS, TLS or the web server is blocking it. It never writes anything into the payment tables.
WiseDiagStep2=2. Test it from your own browser
WiseDiagStep2Desc=Paste the webhook URL into your browser address bar. You should get a JSON answer. Getting nothing at all means something between the internet and PHP is dropping the request (a WAF or Cloudflare rule, which would also block Wise).
WiseDiagStep3=3. Look at the dump directory above
WiseDiagStep3Desc=After steps 1 and 2, reload this page. A new file in the dump directory proves a request reached the receiver; "bootstrap": true in it means it was accepted without signature verification.
WiseDiagStep4=4. Ask Wise to send one
WiseDiagStep4Desc=In the Wise dashboard, re-save the webhook subscription: Wise immediately sends a test notification. Then reload this page and check the dump count and the event count above. If neither moves, the subscription never became active on Wise's side — check that the URL has no query string.
WISE_RUN_SELF_TEST=Run webhook self-test
WiseDiagUrl=URL
WiseDiagResult=Result
WiseDiagBody=Response body
WiseDiagErrHelp=The request did not complete. The URL is not reachable from the server itself: check that the domain resolves, that the SSL certificate is valid, and that no firewall blocks outgoing requests.
WiseDiagHttp200Help=HTTP 200 means the receiver answered. With no verification key yet this is the bootstrap acknowledgement and the delivery was NOT ingested — turn on the IP allowlist or save the signature key.
WiseDiagHttp403Help=HTTP 403 is the IP allowlist rejecting the request, because the self-test comes from the server itself and not from a Wise address. This confirms the allowlist is armed.
WiseDiagHttp404Help=HTTP 404: the receiver file was not found at that URL. Check that the module files were uploaded and that the path matches exactly.
WiseDiagHttp5xxHelp=HTTP 5xx: PHP failed to run the receiver. Check the PHP error log in cPanel (Metrics → Errors).
